        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "| In Splunk you did… | In Grafana you use… |\n|---|---|\n| `eval status=case(avail>=99.8,\"BAU\",…)` / `rangemap` | **Value mappings** (Range / Value / Regex / Special) |\n| Color formatting in table XML | **Thresholds** + cell type *Colored background* |\n| Per-column formatting | **Field overrides** (match by field name) |\n| `<drilldown><link>` | **Data links** on a field or panel |\n| `$click.value$`, `$row.field$` | `${__value.raw}`, `${__data.fields.Field}` |\n| Tokens `$tok$` | Dashboard **variables** `$var` |\n\n**Key idea:** labeling happens at *display time* — the query stays the same, and only the presentation changes.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.3.0-36978054224",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "Splunk → Grafana translation",
      "type": "text"
    },
