      "title": "Ex 1 — Value mappings",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "1. Edit **🛠 Your turn — raw availability**\n2. Find **Value mappings** → *Add value mappings*\n3. Add **Range** 99.8 → 100 = `BAU`, color **blue**\n4. Add **Range** 99 → 99.8 = `Warning`, color **orange**\n5. Add **Range** 0 → 99 = `Critical`, color **red**\n6. Add **Special** *Null + NaN* = `No Data`, color **grey**\n7. Under **Stat styles**, set *Color mode* = **Background gradient**\n8. Under **Standard options**, set *Color scheme* = **From thresholds (by value)**. The panel starts on a fixed *Text* color, and that hides the mapping colors\n\n💡 The query never changed, so the raw number is still there in tooltips and alerts.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.3.0-36978054224",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "Steps: number → BAU / Warning / Critical",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
        "uid": "${DS_TESTDATA}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "fixedColor": "text",
            "mode": "fixed"
          },
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 80
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
